WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.540
This is what happens inside Kairos,
for one borrower, on one day.

2
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.978
Each day, every borrower is re-sorted.
Every move names its rule.

3
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.603
A Bayesian learner tracks reply chances.

4
00:00:21.623 --> 00:00:26.480
On day seven, WhatsApp replies drop.
Kairos isn't told.

5
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.760
By the end of day fourteen,
that segment has moved to SMS.

6
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.980
Learned from replies alone.

7
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.459
Models only suggest.

8
00:00:34.479 --> 00:00:40.780
Aladdin reserves the budget and limits,
then checks every rule again at send time.

9
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.272
Messages go out through each channel.

10
00:00:43.292 --> 00:00:48.325
Delivery and replies come back as webhooks,
and duplicates are ignored.

11
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.480
Kairos: Your EMI was due last week.
Could you pay by Friday?

12
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.380
Sunita: Yes, I'll pay on Friday.

13
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.700
Voice calls run on Sarvam agents.

14
00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.778
Every call comes back
with a disposition and a confidence.

15
00:01:00.798 --> 00:01:04.380
Below a hand-set threshold,
a person reviews it.

16
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.739
Replies climb a ladder:
rules first, then a small model.

17
00:01:08.759 --> 00:01:11.380
Still unsure? A person decides.

18
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.971
People can step in at any moment.

19
00:01:13.991 --> 00:01:19.110
Every action still passes Aladdin,
and lands in the audit log.

20
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:25.448
Same data in, same decisions out.
And we attack it, load it, and test it.

